  {
   "angle": 0,
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "kpi-alpha-label",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "customData": {
    "author": "agent",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "role": "node",
    "tooltip": "Renamed from **Alpha** to **Excess Return**, Aug 2026.\n\nI read that as a precision fix rather than a wording preference: *alpha* implies a risk-adjusted number — return above what the portfolio's exposure would predict — while *excess return* is just return minus benchmark. If the calculation behind this tile is beta-adjusted, the old name was the accurate one and the new one undersells it.",
    "value": "+3.1%"
   },
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "frameId": "screen-dashboard",
   "groupIds": [
    "kpi-alpha-grp"
   ],
   "height": 120,
   "id": "kpi-alpha",
   "isDeleted": false,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "opacity": 100,
   "roughness": 1,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 665930734,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "type": "rectangle",
   "updated": 1,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 0,
   "width": 292,
   "x": 396,
   "y": 152
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "kpi-var-label",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "customData": {
    "author": "agent",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "role": "node",
    "tooltip": "The alert threshold on the console is **2.5%**. This tile says 2.4%.\n\nSo the number everyone looks at is one tenth of a point from firing an alert, and the tile has no way to say so.",
    "value": "2.4%"
   },
